            "review_title": "Review at Tora Tora",
            "review_text": "Jet281491\n3 contributions\n0\nDEFINITELY NOT WORTH GOING!\nAug 2023 • Family\nFirstly, the place isn't as nice as advertised. Food was really mediocre and pricey for what it is. Flavours are mismatched and overpowering. We ordered 9 dishes, only a couple was good. However, the worst of all is the attitude of the management! We ordered a raw octopus starter which was way too salty. Took just a sliver and couldn't eat anymore. Spoke to waitress and she said \"can cancel\", then asked us if we would like to replace with another dish, which we did. We felt bad & ordered another 2 dishes! Then she returned to take the bad octopus away. When the bill arrived, we were charged for the octopus. When queried, shockingly they insisted staff meant \"can't cancel\" & blamed it on language barrier!!! They refused to take it off the bill, reason being it had been served & they had to throw away. I then questioned why else would they ask if we wanted replacement and why did staff returned to take the dish away for which we were going to be charged!! We were so stunned as we are foodies &have been to many restaurants worldwide. Any decent restaurant would waive a VND75000 (US$3)starter if the customer(2 adults, 1 child) spent 1.5mil dong (US$62) but instead they offered 50% discount on the hardly touched dish ie. they insisted to charge us US$1.50. for it. It's almost too HILARIOUS if we weren't so appalled.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 26, 2023",
            "rating": 4.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
